# claude-dotfiles — deny-by-default whitelist
# We track only the portable, sharable subset of ~/.claude/.
# Anything not explicitly un-ignored stays out of git.

# 1) Deny everything at the top level by default.
/*

# 2) Explicit allow-list of tracked top-level entries.
!.gitignore
!README.md
!setup.sh
!CLAUDE.md
!settings.json
!hooks/
!skills/
!commands/
!agents/

# 3) Hard belt-and-suspenders denials.
# Even if a future edit accidentally `git add`s these paths,
# git refuses to stage them.
.credentials.json
.credentials.*.json
*.token
*.key
*secret*
.env
.env.*
**/credentials.json
**/auth.json

# 4) Inside the allow-listed dirs, ignore project-specific files
# that stay local-only. (Inline comments aren't valid here — must be
# their own line.)

# work/ticket-specific shipping command
commands/ship.md

# local hook overrides
hooks/*.local.*

# 5) Editor / OS noise inside tracked dirs.
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
**/*~
**/__pycache__/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
